Even-length space blocks are usually negative when indenting a line;
document-initial blocks instead get positive values. Width, repetition,
preceding braces, tabs, and earlier formatting adjust the strengths.
Frequent even-space blocks and multiple-newline tokens soften indentation
responses. Single-line breaks raise later blank-line responses, whose
baselines also depend on attached punctuation and think delimiters.
Mid-line and escaped-newline spacing have separate strengths. Pairs of
middle dots are strongly negative. Other text stays near zero.
"""
